# Project: Drift

Purpose:
  Define the Declared/Observed/Drift model for detecting divergence
  between the .sdd project model and actual codebase state.

Declared:
  Approved project intent — architecture, domains, modules, components,
  flows, decisions, constraints.

Observed:
  Actual repository/runtime state — source code, tests, config, metrics,
  actual dependencies.

Drift:
  When Declared != Observed, AI MUST create a DRIFT finding and a task
  to reconcile the difference.

DriftSeverity:
  D0: no drift
  D1: minor (typo, naming)
  D2: significant (missing module, wrong dependency)
  D3: critical (architecture violation, security gap)

MinimalModel:
  Every domain/component does NOT need a 500-line document. The minimal
  model is:
    ID
    Paths
    Owns
    DependsOn / UsedBy
    Chain
    Risk

  Everything else lives in the graph and skills.

Rules:
  [PD1] AI MUST detect drift by comparing change impact against the project model.
  [PD2] AI MUST NOT silently update the project model without human approval for significant changes.
  [PD3] Drift findings MUST be created before any model update.
  [PD4] Minimal model prevents context bloat and keeps the project model token-efficient.

GraphDrift:
  When the graph says:
    @payments/refund -> @db/refunds
  but the actual code has:
    @payments/refund -> @redis/cache

  AI MUST:
    1. Detect the drift
    2. Create a DRIFT finding
    3. Create a task to reconcile the graph
    4. NOT silently update the graph without human approval

FallbackDiscovery:
  When the graph says nothing about a node, AI MUST fall back to
  discovery, but MUST NOT silently update the graph:

    GRAPH MISSING
      ↓
    DISCOVER
      ↓
    OBSERVE
      ↓
    DRAFT UPDATE
      ↓
    HUMAN APPROVAL (if significant)
      ↓
    UPDATE GRAPH

DomainGraph:
  Each domain MAY have its own local graph at .sdd/project/<domain>/
  graph.sdd containing only the nodes and edges relevant to that domain.
  The global graph entry point is .sdd/graph/INDEX.sdd.

  Resolution order:
    1. Global graph (.sdd/graph/INDEX.sdd)
    2. Domain graph (.sdd/project/<domain>/graph.sdd)
    3. Component model (.sdd/project/<domain>/<component>.sdd)
    4. Fallback discovery (if all graphs are silent)

Navigation:
  Graph: @../graph/INDEX.sdd
  GraphModel: @../graph/model.sdd
  Dependencies: @dependencies.sdd

